msgid "a number if *x* is a number, else ``None``"
msgstr "eine Zahl, falls *x* eine Zahl ist, andernfalls ``None``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:674
msgid ""
"Return the angle of the line from the turtle's position to (x,y). If *y* is "
"``None``, *x* must be a pair of coordinates, a :class:`Vec2D`, for example "
"as returned by :func:`pos`, or another turtle. The angle is measured from "
"the turtle's start orientation, which depends on the turtle mode, "
"see :func:`mode`."
msgstr ""
"Gib den Winkel der Linie von der Position der Turtle zu (x,y) zurück. Ist "
"*y* ``None``, muss *x* ein Koordinatenpaar sein, ein :class:`Vec2D` – zum "
"Beispiel wie von :func:`pos` zurückgegeben – oder eine andere Turtle. Der "
"Winkel wird von der Startausrichtung der Turtle aus gemessen, die vom Turtle-"
"Modus abhängt, siehe :func:`mode`."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:680
msgid ""
">>> turtle.goto(10, 10)\n"
">>> turtle.towards(0,0)\n"
"225.0"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.goto(10, 10)\n"
">>> turtle.towards(0,0)\n"
"225.0"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:690
msgid "Return the turtle's x coordinate."
msgstr "Gib die x-Koordinate der Turtle zurück."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:692
msgid ""
">>> turtle.home()\n"
">>> turtle.left(50)\n"
">>> turtle.forward(100)\n"
">>> turtle.pos()\n"
"(64.28,76.60)\n"
">>> print(round(turtle.xcor(), 5))\n"
"64.27876"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.home()\n"
">>> turtle.left(50)\n"
">>> turtle.forward(100)\n"
">>> turtle.pos()\n"
"(64.28,76.60)\n"
">>> print(round(turtle.xcor(), 5))\n"
"64.27876"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:706
msgid "Return the turtle's y coordinate."
msgstr "Gib die y-Koordinate der Turtle zurück."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:708
msgid ""
">>> turtle.home()\n"
">>> turtle.left(60)\n"
">>> turtle.forward(100)\n"
">>> print(turtle.pos())\n"
"(50.00,86.60)\n"
">>> print(round(turtle.ycor(), 5))\n"
"86.60254"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.home()\n"
">>> turtle.left(60)\n"
">>> turtle.forward(100)\n"
">>> print(turtle.pos())\n"
"(50.00,86.60)\n"
">>> print(round(turtle.ycor(), 5))\n"
"86.60254"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:722
msgid ""
"Return the turtle's current heading. The value depends on the turtle mode, "
"see :func:`mode`."
msgstr ""
"Gib die aktuelle Ausrichtung der Turtle zurück. Der Wert hängt vom Turtle-"
"Modus ab, siehe :func:`mode`."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:725
msgid ""
">>> turtle.home()\n"
">>> turtle.left(67)\n"
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"67.0"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.home()\n"
">>> turtle.left(67)\n"
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"67.0"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:739
msgid ""
"Return the distance from the turtle to (x,y) in turtle step units. If *y* is "
"``None``, *x* must be a pair of coordinates, a :class:`Vec2D`, for example "
"as returned by :func:`pos`, or another turtle."
msgstr ""
"Gib den Abstand von der Turtle zu (x,y) in Turtle-Schritteinheiten zurück. "
"Ist *y* ``None``, muss *x* ein Koordinatenpaar sein, ein :class:`Vec2D` – "
"zum Beispiel wie von :func:`pos` zurückgegeben – oder eine andere Turtle."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:743
msgid ""
">>> turtle.home()\n"
">>> turtle.distance(30,40)\n"
"50.0\n"
">>> turtle.distance((30,40))\n"
"50.0\n"
">>> joe = Turtle()\n"
">>> joe.forward(77)\n"
">>> turtle.distance(joe)\n"
"77.0"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.home()\n"
">>> turtle.distance(30,40)\n"
"50.0\n"
">>> turtle.distance((30,40))\n"
"50.0\n"
">>> joe = Turtle()\n"
">>> joe.forward(77)\n"
">>> turtle.distance(joe)\n"
"77.0"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:758
