msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:854
msgid "\"pendown\": ``True`` or ``False``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:855
msgid "\"pencolor\": a color string or a color tuple"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:856
msgid "\"fillcolor\": a color string or a color tuple"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:857
msgid "\"pensize\": a positive number"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:858
msgid "\"speed\": a number from 0 to 10"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:859
msgid "\"resizemode\": \"auto\", \"user\" or \"noresize\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:860
msgid "\"stretchfactor\": a pair of positive numbers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:861
msgid "\"shearfactor\": a number"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:862
msgid "\"outline\": a positive number"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:863
msgid "\"tilt\": a number"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:865
msgid ""
"Such a dictionary can be passed as *pen* to restore a former pen state. The "
"attributes can also be given as keyword arguments, which can be used to set "
"several of them in one statement."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:869
msgid ""
">>> turtle.pen(fillcolor=\"black\", pencolor=\"red\", pensize=10)\n"
">>> turtle.pen()\n"
"{'shown': True, 'pendown': True, 'pencolor': 'red', 'fillcolor': 'black',\n"
" 'pensize': 10, 'speed': 9, 'resizemode': 'noresize',\n"
" 'stretchfactor': (1.0, 1.0), 'shearfactor': 0.0, 'outline': 1,\n"
" 'tilt': 0.0}\n"
">>> penstate = turtle.pen()\n"
">>> turtle.color(\"yellow\", \"\")\n"
">>> turtle.penup()\n"
">>> turtle.pen()[\"pencolor\"]\n"
"'yellow'\n"
">>> # restore the saved pen state, but with a green fill\n"
">>> turtle.pen(penstate, fillcolor=\"green\")\n"
">>> turtle.pen()[\"pencolor\"]\n"
"'red'\n"
">>> turtle.pen()[\"fillcolor\"]\n"
"'green'"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:893
msgid "Return ``True`` if the pen is down, ``False`` if it's up."
msgstr ""
"Gib ``True`` zurück, wenn der Stift unten ist, ``False``, wenn er oben ist."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:895
msgid ""
">>> turtle.penup()\n"
">>> turtle.isdown()\n"
"False\n"
">>> turtle.pendown()\n"
">>> turtle.isdown()\n"
"True"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.penup()\n"
">>> turtle.isdown()\n"
"False\n"
">>> turtle.pendown()\n"
">>> turtle.isdown()\n"
"True"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:907
msgid "Color control"
msgstr "Farbkontrolle"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:913
msgid "Return or set the pencolor."
msgstr "Gib die Stiftfarbe zurück oder setze sie."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:915 ../../library/turtle.rst:967
#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1624
msgid "Four input formats are allowed:"
msgstr "Vier Eingabeformate sind erlaubt:"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:917
msgid "``pencolor()``"
msgstr "``pencolor()``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:918
msgid ""
"Return the current pencolor as color specification string or as a tuple (see "
"example).  May be used as input to "
"another :func:`color`, :func:`pencolor`, :func:`fillcolor` "
"or :func:`bgcolor` call."
msgstr ""
"Gib die aktuelle Stiftfarbe als Farbangabe-Zeichenkette oder als Tupel "
"zurück (siehe Beispiel). Kann als Eingabe für einen weiteren Aufruf "
"von :func:`color`, :func:`pencolor`, :func:`fillcolor` oder :func:`bgcolor` "
"verwendet werden."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:923
msgid "``pencolor(colorstring)``"
msgstr "``pencolor(colorstring)``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:924
msgid ""
"Set the pencolor to *colorstring*, which is a Tk color specification string, "
"such as ``\"red\"``, ``\"yellow\"``, or ``\"#33cc8c\"``."
msgstr ""
"Setze die Stiftfarbe auf *colorstring*, was ein Tk-Farbangabe-String ist, "
"wie zum Beispiel ``\"red\"``, ``\"yellow\"`` oder ``\"#33cc8c\"``."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:927
msgid "``pencolor((r, g, b))``"
msgstr "``pencolor((r, g, b))``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:928
msgid ""
"Set the pencolor to the RGB color represented by the tuple of *r*, *g*, and "
"*b*. Each of *r*, *g*, and *b* must be between 0 and colormode, where "
"colormode is either 1.0 or 255 (see :func:`colormode`)."
msgstr ""
"Setze die Stiftfarbe auf die durch das Tupel aus *r*, *g* und *b* "
"dargestellte RGB-Farbe. Jeder der Werte *r*, *g* und *b* muss im Bereich "
"0..colormode liegen, wobei colormode entweder 1.0 oder 255 ist "
"(siehe :func:`colormode`)."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:932
msgid "``pencolor(r, g, b)``"
msgstr "``pencolor(r, g, b)``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:933
msgid ""
"Set the pencolor to the RGB color represented by *r*, *g*, and *b*. Each of "
"*r*, *g*, and *b* must be between 0 and colormode."
msgstr ""
"Setze die Stiftfarbe auf die durch *r*, *g* und *b* dargestellte RGB-Farbe. "
"Jeder der Werte *r*, *g* und *b* muss im Bereich 0..colormode liegen."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:936
msgid ""
"If the turtle shape is a polygon, the outline of that polygon is drawn with "
"the newly set pencolor."
msgstr ""
"Ist die Form der Turtle ein Polygon, wird der Umriss dieses Polygons mit der "
"neu gesetzten Stiftfarbe gezeichnet."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:939
msgid ""
">>> colormode()\n"
"1.0\n"
">>> turtle.pencolor()\n"
"'red'\n"
">>> turtle.pencolor(\"brown\")\n"
">>> turtle.pencolor()\n"
"'brown'\n"
">>> tup = (0.2, 0.8, 0.55)\n"
">>> turtle.pencolor(tup)\n"
">>> turtle.pencolor()\n"
"(0.2, 0.8, 0.5490196078431373)\n"
">>> colormode(255)\n"
">>> turtle.pencolor()\n"
"(51.0, 204.0, 140.0)\n"
">>> turtle.pencolor('#32c18f')\n"
">>> turtle.pencolor()\n"
"(50.0, 193.0, 143.0)"
msgstr ""
">>> colormode()\n"
"1.0\n"
">>> turtle.pencolor()\n"
"'red'\n"
">>> turtle.pencolor(\"brown\")\n"
">>> turtle.pencolor()\n"
"'brown'\n"
">>> tup = (0.2, 0.8, 0.55)\n"
">>> turtle.pencolor(tup)\n"
">>> turtle.pencolor()\n"
"(0.2, 0.8, 0.5490196078431373)\n"
">>> colormode(255)\n"
">>> turtle.pencolor()\n"
"(51.0, 204.0, 140.0)\n"
">>> turtle.pencolor('#32c18f')\n"
">>> turtle.pencolor()\n"
"(50.0, 193.0, 143.0)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:965
msgid "Return or set the fillcolor."
msgstr "Gib die Füllfarbe zurück oder setze sie."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:969
msgid "``fillcolor()``"
msgstr "``fillcolor()``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:970
msgid ""
"Return the current fillcolor as color specification string, possibly in "
"tuple format (see example).  May be used as input to "
"another :func:`color`, :func:`pencolor`, :func:`fillcolor` "
"or :func:`bgcolor` call."
msgstr ""
"Gib die aktuelle Füllfarbe als Farbangabe-Zeichenkette zurück, "
"möglicherweise im Tupel-Format (siehe Beispiel). Kann als Eingabe für einen "
"weiteren Aufruf von :func:`color`, :func:`pencolor`, :func:`fillcolor` "
"oder :func:`bgcolor` verwendet werden."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:975
msgid "``fillcolor(colorstring)``"
msgstr "``fillcolor(colorstring)``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:976
msgid ""
"Set the fillcolor to *colorstring*, which is a Tk color specification "
"string, such as ``\"red\"``, ``\"yellow\"``, or ``\"#33cc8c\"``."
msgstr ""
"Setze die Füllfarbe auf *colorstring*, was ein Tk-Farbangabe-String ist, wie "
"zum Beispiel ``\"red\"``, ``\"yellow\"`` oder ``\"#33cc8c\"``."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:979
msgid "``fillcolor((r, g, b))``"
msgstr "``fillcolor((r, g, b))``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:980
msgid ""
"Set the fillcolor to the RGB color represented by the tuple of *r*, *g*, and "
"*b*. Each of *r*, *g*, and *b* must be between 0 and colormode, where "
"colormode is either 1.0 or 255 (see :func:`colormode`)."
msgstr ""
"Setze die Füllfarbe auf die durch das Tupel aus *r*, *g* und *b* "
"dargestellte RGB-Farbe. Jeder der Werte *r*, *g* und *b* muss im Bereich "
"0..colormode liegen, wobei colormode entweder 1.0 oder 255 ist "
"(siehe :func:`colormode`)."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:984
msgid "``fillcolor(r, g, b)``"
msgstr "``fillcolor(r, g, b)``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:985
msgid ""
"Set the fillcolor to the RGB color represented by *r*, *g*, and *b*. Each of "
"*r*, *g*, and *b* must be between 0 and colormode."
msgstr ""
"Setze die Füllfarbe auf die durch *r*, *g* und *b* dargestellte RGB-Farbe. "
"Jeder der Werte *r*, *g* und *b* muss im Bereich 0..colormode liegen."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:988
msgid ""
"If the turtle shape is a polygon, the interior of that polygon is drawn with "
"the newly set fillcolor."
msgstr ""
"Ist die Form der Turtle ein Polygon, wird das Innere dieses Polygons mit der "
"neu gesetzten Füllfarbe gezeichnet."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:991
msgid ""
">>> turtle.fillcolor(\"violet\")\n"
">>> turtle.fillcolor()\n"
"'violet'\n"
">>> turtle.pencolor()\n"
"(50.0, 193.0, 143.0)\n"
">>> turtle.fillcolor((50, 193, 143))  # Integers, not floats\n"
">>> turtle.fillcolor()\n"
"(50.0, 193.0, 143.0)\n"
">>> turtle.fillcolor('#ffffff')\n"
">>> turtle.fillcolor()\n"
"(255.0, 255.0, 255.0)"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.fillcolor(\"violet\")\n"
">>> turtle.fillcolor()\n"
"'violet'\n"
">>> turtle.pencolor()\n"
"(50.0, 193.0, 143.0)\n"
">>> turtle.fillcolor((50, 193, 143))  # Integers, not floats\n"
">>> turtle.fillcolor()\n"
"(50.0, 193.0, 143.0)\n"
">>> turtle.fillcolor('#ffffff')\n"
">>> turtle.fillcolor()\n"
"(255.0, 255.0, 255.0)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1012
msgid "Return or set the pencolor and fillcolor."
msgstr "Gib die Stiftfarbe und die Füllfarbe zurück oder setze sie."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1014
msgid ""
"Several input formats are allowed. They use 0 to 3 arguments as follows:"
msgstr ""
"Mehrere Eingabeformate sind erlaubt. Sie verwenden dabei 0 bis 3 Argumente "
"wie folgt:"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1017
msgid "``color()``"
msgstr "``color()``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1018
msgid ""
"Return the current pencolor and the current fillcolor as a pair of color "
"specification strings or tuples as returned by :func:`pencolor` "
"and :func:`fillcolor`."
msgstr ""
"Gib die aktuelle Stiftfarbe und die aktuelle Füllfarbe als Paar von "
"Farbangabe-Strings oder Tupeln zurück, wie sie von :func:`pencolor` "
"und :func:`fillcolor` zurückgegeben werden."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1022
msgid "``color(colorstring)``, ``color((r,g,b))``, ``color(r,g,b)``"
msgstr "``color(colorstring)``, ``color((r,g,b))``, ``color(r,g,b)``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1023
msgid ""
"Inputs as in :func:`pencolor`. Set both the pencolor and the fillcolor to "
"the given value."
msgstr ""
"Eingaben wie bei :func:`pencolor`, setzt sowohl fillcolor als auch pencolor "
"auf den angegebenen Wert."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1026
msgid ""
"``color(colorstring1, colorstring2)``, ``color((r1,g1,b1), (r2,g2,b2))``"
msgstr ""
"``color(colorstring1, colorstring2)``, ``color((r1,g1,b1), (r2,g2,b2))``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1027
msgid ""
"Equivalent to ``pencolor(colorstring1)`` and ``fillcolor(colorstring2)`` and "
"analogously if the other input format is used."
msgstr ""
"Entspricht ``pencolor(colorstring1)`` und ``fillcolor(colorstring2)`` und "
"analog, wenn das andere Eingabeformat verwendet wird."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1030
msgid ""
"If the turtle shape is a polygon, the outline and interior of that polygon "
"are drawn with the newly set colors."
msgstr ""
"Ist die Form der Turtle ein Polygon, werden Umriss und Inneres dieses "
"Polygons mit den neu gesetzten Farben gezeichnet."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1033
msgid ""
">>> turtle.color(\"red\", \"green\")\n"
">>> turtle.color()\n"
"('red', 'green')\n"
">>> color(\"#285078\", \"#a0c8f0\")\n"
">>> color()\n"
"((40.0, 80.0, 120.0), (160.0, 200.0, 240.0))"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.color(\"red\", \"green\")\n"
">>> turtle.color()\n"
"('red', 'green')\n"
">>> color(\"#285078\", \"#a0c8f0\")\n"
">>> color()\n"
"((40.0, 80.0, 120.0), (160.0, 200.0, 240.0))"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1044
msgid "See also: Screen method :func:`colormode`."
msgstr "Siehe auch: Screen-Methode :func:`colormode`."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1048
msgid "Filling"
msgstr "Füllen"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1059
msgid "Return ``True`` if the turtle is filling, ``False`` otherwise."
msgstr ""
"Gib ``True`` zurück, wenn die Turtle gerade füllt, andernfalls ``False``."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1061
msgid ""
">>> turtle.begin_fill()\n"
">>> if turtle.filling():\n"
"...    turtle.pensize(5)\n"
"... else:\n"
"...    turtle.pensize(3)"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.begin_fill()\n"
">>> if turtle.filling():\n"
"...    turtle.pensize(5)\n"
"... else:\n"
"...    turtle.pensize(3)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1073
msgid "Fill the shape drawn in the :keyword:`with` block."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1075
msgid ""
">>> turtle.color(\"black\", \"red\")\n"
">>> with turtle.fill():\n"
"...     turtle.circle(80)"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.color(\"black\", \"red\")\n"
">>> with turtle.fill():\n"
"...     turtle.circle(80)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1082
msgid ""
":func:`fill` is a :term:`context manager`, so using it is the same as "
"calling :func:`begin_fill` before the block and :func:`end_fill` after it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1085 ../../library/turtle.rst:1111
msgid ""
">>> turtle.color(\"black\", \"red\")\n"
">>> turtle.begin_fill()\n"
">>> turtle.circle(80)\n"
">>> turtle.end_fill()"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.color(\"black\", \"red\")\n"
">>> turtle.begin_fill()\n"
">>> turtle.circle(80)\n"
">>> turtle.end_fill()"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1098
msgid ""
"Call just before drawing a shape to be filled. The shape is filled by the "
"next call to :func:`end_fill`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1104
msgid "Fill the shape drawn after the last call to :func:`begin_fill`."
msgstr ""
"Fülle die Form, die seit dem letzten Aufruf von :func:`begin_fill` "
"gezeichnet wurde."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1106
msgid ""
"If the shape crosses itself or several shapes overlap, whether the "
"overlapping parts are filled depends on the operating system, the type of "
"overlap and how many there are. For example, the turtle star above may be "
"either all yellow or have some white regions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1121
msgid "More drawing control"
msgstr "Mehr Zeichenkontrolle"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1125
msgid ""
"Delete the turtle's drawings and re-center the turtle. The turtle's settings "
"are restored to their default values."
msgstr ""
"Lösche die Zeichnungen der Turtle und zentriere die Turtle neu. Die "
"Einstellungen der Turtle werden auf ihre Standardwerte zurückgesetzt."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1128
msgid ""
">>> turtle.goto(0,-22)\n"
">>> turtle.left(100)\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(0.00,-22.00)\n"
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"100.0\n"
">>> turtle.reset()\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(0.00,0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"0.0"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.goto(0,-22)\n"
">>> turtle.left(100)\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(0.00,-22.00)\n"
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"100.0\n"
">>> turtle.reset()\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(0.00,0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"0.0"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1146
msgid ""
"Delete the turtle's drawings from the screen. The state and position of the "
"turtle as well as the drawings of other turtles are not affected."
msgstr ""
"Lösche die Zeichnungen der Turtle vom Bildschirm. Zustand und Position der "
"Turtle sowie die Zeichnungen anderer Turtles bleiben davon unberührt."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1152
msgid "an object"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1154 ../../library/turtle.rst:1850
#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1959 ../../library/turtle.rst:1960
#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1971 ../../library/turtle.rst:1972
#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2069 ../../library/turtle.rst:2158
#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2204 ../../library/turtle.rst:2260
msgid "a string"
msgstr "eine Zeichenkette"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1155
msgid "a tuple of a string, an integer and a string"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1157
msgid ""
"Write text at the current turtle position. The text is the string "
"representation of *arg*. *align* is one of the strings \"left\", \"center\" "
"or \"right\" and says how the text is placed relative to the turtle "
"position. *font* is a triple of font name, font size and font type. If "
"*move* is ``True``, the pen is moved to the bottom-right corner of the text."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1163
msgid ""
">>> turtle.write(\"Home = \", True, align=\"center\")\n"
">>> turtle.write((0,0), True)"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.write(\"Home = \", True, align=\"center\")\n"
">>> turtle.write((0,0), True)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1171
msgid "Turtle state"
msgstr "Turtle-Status"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1174
msgid "Visibility"
msgstr "Sichtbarkeit"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1179
msgid "Make the turtle invisible. If the pen is down, movement still draws."
msgstr ""
"Mache die Turtle unsichtbar. Ist der Stift unten, zeichnet eine Bewegung "
"weiterhin."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1185
msgid "Make the turtle visible."
msgstr "Mache die Turtle sichtbar."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1190
msgid "Return ``True`` if the turtle is visible, ``False`` if it's hidden."
msgstr ""
"Gib ``True`` zurück, wenn die Turtle sichtbar ist, ``False``, wenn sie "
"versteckt ist."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1192
msgid ""
">>> turtle.hideturtle()\n"
">>> turtle.isvisible()\n"
"False\n"
">>> turtle.showturtle()\n"
">>> turtle.isvisible()\n"
"True"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.hideturtle()\n"
">>> turtle.isvisible()\n"
"False\n"
">>> turtle.showturtle()\n"
">>> turtle.isvisible()\n"
"True"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1204
msgid "Appearance"
msgstr "Erscheinungsbild"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1208 ../../library/turtle.rst:1228
#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1659 ../../library/turtle.rst:1874
#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1993
msgid "a string or ``None``"
msgstr "eine Zeichenkette oder ``None``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1210
msgid ""
"Set the turtle shape to the named shape. If *name* is not given, return the "
"name of the current shape. The shape must exist in "
"the :class:`TurtleScreen`'s shape dictionary. Initially there are the "
"following shapes: \"arrow\", \"turtle\", \"circle\", \"square\", "
"\"triangle\" and \"classic\". To add shapes, see the :class:`Screen` "
"method :func:`register_shape`."
msgstr ""
"Setze die Form der Turtle auf die Form mit dem angegebenen Namen. Wird "
"*name* nicht angegeben, wird der Name der aktuellen Form zurückgegeben. Die "
"Form muss im Formen-Dictionary des :class:`TurtleScreen` vorhanden sein. "
"Anfangs gibt es die folgenden Formen: \"arrow\", \"turtle\", \"circle\", "
"\"square\", \"triangle\" und \"classic\". Um Formen hinzuzufügen, siehe "
"die :class:`Screen`-Methode :func:`register_shape`."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1216
msgid ""
">>> turtle.shape()\n"
"'classic'\n"
">>> turtle.shape(\"turtle\")\n"
">>> turtle.shape()\n"
"'turtle'"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.shape()\n"
"'classic'\n"
">>> turtle.shape(\"turtle\")\n"
">>> turtle.shape()\n"
"'turtle'"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1230
msgid ""
"Set the resizemode to \"auto\", \"user\" or \"noresize\". If *rmode* is not "
"given, return the current resizemode. The different resizemodes have the "
"following effects:"
msgstr ""
"Setze resizemode auf \"auto\", \"user\" oder \"noresize\". Wird *rmode* "
"nicht angegeben, wird der aktuelle resizemode zurückgegeben. Die "
"verschiedenen resizemodes haben folgende Auswirkungen:"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1234
msgid ""
"\"auto\": the turtle is resized according to the value of :func:`pensize`."
msgstr ""
"\"auto\": Die Größe der Turtle richtet sich nach dem Wert "
"von :func:`pensize`."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1235
msgid ""
"\"user\": the turtle is resized according to the stretch factors and outline "
"width, which are set by :func:`shapesize`."
msgstr ""
"\"user\": Die Größe der Turtle richtet sich nach den Streckfaktoren und der "
"Umrissbreite, die :func:`shapesize` setzt."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1237
msgid "\"noresize\": the turtle is not resized."
msgstr "\"noresize\": Die Größe der Turtle wird nicht verändert."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1239
msgid ""
"``resizemode(\"user\")`` is called by :func:`shapesize` when used with "
"arguments."
msgstr ""
"``resizemode(\"user\")`` wird von :func:`shapesize` aufgerufen, wenn es mit "
"Argumenten verwendet wird."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1242
msgid ""
">>> turtle.resizemode()\n"
"'noresize'\n"
">>> turtle.resizemode(\"auto\")\n"
">>> turtle.resizemode()\n"
"'auto'"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.resizemode()\n"
"'noresize'\n"
">>> turtle.resizemode(\"auto\")\n"
">>> turtle.resizemode()\n"
"'auto'"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1259
msgid ""
"Return or set the turtle's stretch factors and outline width. If no "
"arguments are given, return the current values. Otherwise set resizemode to "
"\"user\", so that the turtle is displayed stretched according to its stretch "
"factors:"
msgstr ""
"Gib die Streckfaktoren und die Umrissbreite der Turtle zurück oder setze "
"sie. Werden keine Argumente angegeben, werden die aktuellen Werte "
"zurückgegeben. Andernfalls wird resizemode auf \"user\" gesetzt, sodass die "
"Turtle entsprechend ihren Streckfaktoren gestreckt dargestellt wird:"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1264
msgid "*stretch_wid*: the stretch factor perpendicular to the turtle's heading"
msgstr "*stretch_wid*: der Streckfaktor senkrecht zur Ausrichtung der Turtle"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1265
msgid ""
"*stretch_len*: the stretch factor in the direction of the turtle's heading"
msgstr "*stretch_len*: der Streckfaktor in Richtung der Ausrichtung der Turtle"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1267
msgid "*outline*: the width of the shape's outline"
msgstr "*outline*: die Breite des Umrisses der Form"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1269
msgid ""
"For example, ``shapesize(2, 1)`` makes the turtle twice as wide without "
"changing its length. If only *stretch_wid* is given, *stretch_len* is set to "
"the same value."
msgstr ""
"``shapesize(2, 1)`` macht die Turtle zum Beispiel doppelt so breit, ohne "
"ihre Länge zu ändern. Wird nur *stretch_wid* angegeben, wird *stretch_len* "
"auf denselben Wert gesetzt."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1273
msgid ""
">>> turtle.shapesize()\n"
"(1.0, 1.0, 1)\n"
">>> turtle.resizemode(\"user\")\n"
">>> turtle.shapesize(5, 5, 12)\n"
">>> turtle.shapesize()\n"
"(5, 5, 12)\n"
">>> turtle.shapesize(outline=8)\n"
">>> turtle.shapesize()\n"
"(5, 5, 8)"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.shapesize()\n"
"(1.0, 1.0, 1)\n"
">>> turtle.resizemode(\"user\")\n"
">>> turtle.shapesize(5, 5, 12)\n"
">>> turtle.shapesize()\n"
"(5, 5, 12)\n"
">>> turtle.shapesize(outline=8)\n"
">>> turtle.shapesize()\n"
"(5, 5, 8)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1291
msgid ""
"Return or set the current shear factor. Shearing slants the turtle shape, "
"like the slant of italic letters. The shear factor says how much it is "
"slanted: 0 is not slanted at all, and the larger the number, the stronger "
"the slant. Negative numbers slant the other way. If *shear* is not given, "
"return the current shear factor. Otherwise slant the turtle shape "
"accordingly and set resizemode to \"user\". The turtle's heading does not "
"change. Precisely, the shear factor is the tangent of the shear angle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1299
msgid ""
">>> turtle.shape(\"circle\")\n"
">>> turtle.shapesize(5,2)\n"
">>> turtle.shearfactor(0.5)\n"
">>> turtle.shearfactor()\n"
"0.5"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.shape(\"circle\")\n"
">>> turtle.shapesize(5,2)\n"
">>> turtle.shearfactor(0.5)\n"
">>> turtle.shearfactor()\n"
"0.5"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1313
msgid ""
"Turn the turtle shape by *angle* from its current tilt angle. The turtle's "
"heading does not change, so the turtle keeps moving in the same direction. "
"See :func:`tiltangle`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1317
msgid ""
">>> turtle.reset()\n"
">>> turtle.shape(\"circle\")\n"
">>> turtle.shapesize(5,2)\n"
">>> turtle.tilt(30)\n"
">>> turtle.fd(50)\n"
">>> turtle.tilt(30)\n"
">>> turtle.fd(50)"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.reset()\n"
">>> turtle.shape(\"circle\")\n"
">>> turtle.shapesize(5,2)\n"
">>> turtle.tilt(30)\n"
">>> turtle.fd(50)\n"
">>> turtle.tilt(30)\n"
">>> turtle.fd(50)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1333
msgid ""
"Return or set the current tilt angle. The tilt angle is the angle between "
"the direction the turtle shape points in and the direction the turtle moves "
"in. Normally the shape points in the direction of movement, so the tilt "
"angle is 0. If *angle* is given, turn the turtle shape to that tilt angle, "
"no matter what it was before, and set resizemode to \"user\". The turtle's "
"heading does not change. If *angle* is not given, return the current tilt "
"angle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1341
msgid ""
">>> turtle.reset()\n"
">>> turtle.shape(\"circle\")\n"
">>> turtle.shapesize(5,2)\n"
">>> turtle.tilt(45)\n"
">>> turtle.tiltangle()\n"
"45.0"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.reset()\n"
">>> turtle.shape(\"circle\")\n"
">>> turtle.shapesize(5,2)\n"
">>> turtle.tilt(45)\n"
">>> turtle.tiltangle()\n"
"45.0"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1359
msgid ""
"Return or set the transformation matrix of the turtle shape. The matrix "
"combines the stretch factors, the shear factor and the tilt angle of the "
"turtle shape into four numbers: *t11* and *t12* form its first row, *t21* "
"and *t22* its second. If none of them are given, return the current matrix "
"as a tuple of four numbers. Otherwise set the given elements and update the "
"stretch factors, shear factor and tilt angle accordingly. ``t11 * t22 - t12 "
"* t21`` must not be zero, otherwise an error is raised."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1367
msgid ""
">>> turtle = Turtle()\n"
">>> turtle.shape(\"square\")\n"
">>> turtle.shapesize(4,2)\n"
">>> turtle.shearfactor(-0.5)\n"
">>> turtle.shapetransform()\n"
"(4.0, -1.0, -0.0, 2.0)"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle = Turtle()\n"
">>> turtle.shape(\"square\")\n"
">>> turtle.shapesize(4,2)\n"
">>> turtle.shearfactor(-0.5)\n"
">>> turtle.shapetransform()\n"
"(4.0, -1.0, -0.0, 2.0)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1380
msgid ""
"Return the points that form the outline of the current turtle shape as a "
"tuple of ``(x, y)`` coordinate pairs. These points can be used to define a "
"new shape or parts of a :ref:`compound shape <compound-shapes>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1384
msgid ""
">>> turtle.shape(\"square\")\n"
">>> turtle.shapetransform(4, -1, 0, 2)\n"
">>> turtle.get_shapepoly()\n"
"((50, -20), (30, 20), (-50, 20), (-30, -20))"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.shape(\"square\")\n"
">>> turtle.shapetransform(4, -1, 0, 2)\n"
">>> turtle.get_shapepoly()\n"
"((50, -20), (30, 20), (-50, 20), (-30, -20))"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1394
msgid "Using events"
msgstr "Ereignisse verwenden"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1399 ../../library/turtle.rst:1899
msgid "a function with two arguments or ``None``"
msgstr "eine Funktion mit zwei Argumenten oder ``None``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1401 ../../library/turtle.rst:1901
msgid "a boolean or ``None``"
msgstr "ein Wahrheitswert oder ``None``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1403
msgid ""
"Bind *fun* to mouse-click events on this turtle. *fun* is called with the "
"coordinates of the clicked point on the canvas. If *fun* is ``None``, "
"existing bindings are removed. *btn* is the number of the mouse button and "
"defaults to 1, the left mouse button. If *add* is ``True``, a new binding is "
"added, otherwise it replaces a former binding. Example for the anonymous "
"turtle, that is, the procedural way:"
msgstr ""
"Binde *fun* an Mausklick-Ereignisse auf dieser Turtle. *fun* wird mit den "
"Koordinaten des angeklickten Punktes auf der Leinwand aufgerufen. Ist *fun* "
"``None``, werden bestehende Bindungen entfernt. *btn* ist die Nummer der "
"Maustaste und ist standardmäßig 1, die linke Maustaste. Ist *add* ``True``, "
"wird eine neue Bindung hinzugefügt, andernfalls ersetzt sie eine frühere "
"Bindung. Beispiel für die anonyme Turtle, also der prozedurale Weg:"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1410
msgid ""
">>> def turn(x, y):\n"
"...     left(180)\n"
"...\n"
">>> onclick(turn)  # Now clicking into the turtle will turn it.\n"
">>> onclick(None)  # event-binding will be removed"
msgstr ""
">>> def turn(x, y):\n"
"...     left(180)\n"
"...\n"
">>> onclick(turn)  # Now clicking into the turtle will turn it.\n"
">>> onclick(None)  # event-binding will be removed"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1422 ../../library/turtle.rst:1447
msgid ""
"a function with two arguments which will be called with the coordinates of "
"the clicked point on the canvas"
msgstr ""
"eine Funktion mit zwei Argumenten, die mit den Koordinaten des angeklickten "
"Punkts auf der Zeichenfläche aufgerufen wird"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1424 ../../library/turtle.rst:1449
msgid "number of the mouse-button, defaults to 1 (left mouse button)"
msgstr "Nummer der Maustaste, standardmäßig 1 (linke Maustaste)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1425 ../../library/turtle.rst:1450
msgid ""
"``True`` or ``False`` -- if ``True``, a new binding will be added, otherwise "
"it will replace a former binding"
msgstr ""
"``True`` oder ``False`` -- ist es ``True``, wird eine neue Bindung "
"hinzugefügt, andernfalls ersetzt sie eine vorherige Bindung"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1428
msgid ""
"Bind *fun* to mouse-button-release events on this turtle.  If *fun* is "
"``None``, existing bindings are removed."
msgstr ""
"Binde *fun* an Loslassen-der-Maustaste-Ereignisse dieser Turtle. Ist *fun* "
"``None``, werden bestehende Bindungen entfernt."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1431
msgid ""
">>> class MyTurtle(Turtle):\n"
"...     def glow(self,x,y):\n"
"...         self.fillcolor(\"red\")\n"
"...     def unglow(self,x,y):\n"
"...         self.fillcolor(\"\")\n"
"...\n"
">>> turtle = MyTurtle()\n"
">>> turtle.onclick(turtle.glow)     # clicking on turtle turns fillcolor "
"red,\n"
">>> turtle.onrelease(turtle.unglow) # releasing turns it to transparent."
msgstr ""
">>> class MyTurtle(Turtle):\n"
"...     def glow(self,x,y):\n"
"...         self.fillcolor(\"red\")\n"
"...     def unglow(self,x,y):\n"
"...         self.fillcolor(\"\")\n"
"...\n"
">>> turtle = MyTurtle()\n"
">>> turtle.onclick(turtle.glow)     # clicking on turtle turns fillcolor "
"red,\n"
">>> turtle.onrelease(turtle.unglow) # releasing turns it to transparent."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1453
msgid ""
"Bind *fun* to mouse-move events on this turtle.  If *fun* is ``None``, "
"existing bindings are removed."
msgstr ""
"Binde *fun* an Mausbewegungs-Ereignisse dieser Turtle. Ist *fun* ``None``, "
"werden bestehende Bindungen entfernt."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1456
msgid ""
"Remark: Every sequence of mouse-move-events on a turtle is preceded by a "
"mouse-click event on that turtle."
msgstr ""
"Anmerkung: Jeder Abfolge von Mausbewegungs-Ereignissen auf einer Turtle geht "
"ein Mausklick-Ereignis auf dieser Turtle voraus."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1459
msgid ">>> turtle.ondrag(turtle.goto)"
msgstr ">>> turtle.ondrag(turtle.goto)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1464
msgid ""
"Subsequently, clicking and dragging the Turtle will move it across the "
"screen thereby producing handdrawings (if pen is down)."
msgstr ""
"Anschließend bewegt das Klicken und Ziehen der Turtle diese über den "
"Bildschirm und erzeugt dabei Handzeichnungen (wenn der Stift unten ist)."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1469
msgid "Special Turtle methods"
msgstr "Spezielle Turtle-Methoden"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1473
msgid ""
"Record the vertices of a polygon drawn in the :keyword:`with` block. The "
"first and last vertices will be connected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1476
msgid ""
">>> with turtle.poly():\n"
"...     turtle.forward(100)\n"
"...     turtle.right(60)\n"
"...     turtle.forward(100)"
msgstr ""
">>> with turtle.poly():\n"
"...     turtle.forward(100)\n"
"...     turtle.right(60)\n"
"...     turtle.forward(100)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1484
msgid ""
":func:`poly` is a :term:`context manager`, so using it is the same as "
"calling :func:`begin_poly` before the block and :func:`end_poly` after it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1487
msgid ""
">>> turtle.begin_poly()\n"
">>> turtle.forward(100)\n"
">>> turtle.right(60)\n"
">>> turtle.forward(100)\n"
">>> turtle.end_poly()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1501
msgid ""
"Start recording the vertices of a polygon. The current turtle position is "
"the first vertex of the polygon."
msgstr ""
"Beginne mit dem Aufzeichnen der Eckpunkte eines Polygons. Die aktuelle "
"Position der Turtle ist der erste Eckpunkt des Polygons."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1507
msgid ""
"Stop recording the vertices of a polygon. The current turtle position is the "
"last vertex of the polygon. This will be connected with the first vertex."
msgstr ""
"Beende das Aufzeichnen der Eckpunkte eines Polygons. Die aktuelle Position "
"der Turtle ist der letzte Eckpunkt des Polygons. Dieser wird mit dem ersten "
"Eckpunkt verbunden."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1513
msgid "Return the last recorded polygon."
msgstr "Gib das zuletzt aufgezeichnete Polygon zurück."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1515
msgid ""
">>> turtle.home()\n"
">>> turtle.begin_poly()\n"
">>> turtle.fd(100)\n"
">>> turtle.left(20)\n"
">>> turtle.fd(30)\n"
">>> turtle.left(60)\n"
">>> turtle.fd(50)\n"
">>> turtle.end_poly()\n"
">>> p = turtle.get_poly()\n"
">>> register_shape(\"myFavouriteShape\", p)"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.home()\n"
">>> turtle.begin_poly()\n"
">>> turtle.fd(100)\n"
">>> turtle.left(20)\n"
">>> turtle.fd(30)\n"
">>> turtle.left(60)\n"
">>> turtle.fd(50)\n"
">>> turtle.end_poly()\n"
">>> p = turtle.get_poly()\n"
">>> register_shape(\"myFavouriteShape\", p)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1532
msgid ""
"Create and return a clone of the turtle. The clone has the same position, "
"heading and turtle properties."
msgstr ""
"Erstelle und gib einen Klon der Turtle mit derselben Position, Ausrichtung "
"und denselben Turtle-Eigenschaften zurück."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1535
msgid ""
">>> leonel = Turtle()\n"
">>> marco = leonel.clone()"
msgstr ""
">>> leonel = Turtle()\n"
">>> marco = leonel.clone()"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1545
msgid "Return the Turtle object itself."
msgstr "Gib das Turtle-Objekt selbst zurück."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1547
msgid ""
"Call ``getturtle()`` to get the turtle used by functions such "
"as :func:`forward` and :func:`left`:"
msgstr ""
"Rufe ``getturtle()`` auf, um die Turtle zu bekommen, die Funktionen "
"wie :func:`forward` und :func:`left` verwenden:"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1550
msgid ""
">>> pet = getturtle()\n"
">>> pet.fd(50)\n"
">>> pet\n"
"<turtle.Turtle object at 0x...>"
msgstr ""
">>> pet = getturtle()\n"
">>> pet.fd(50)\n"
">>> pet\n"
"<turtle.Turtle object at 0x...>"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1561
msgid ""
"Return the :class:`TurtleScreen` object the turtle is drawing on. "
"TurtleScreen methods can then be called for that object."
msgstr ""
"Gib das :class:`TurtleScreen`-Objekt zurück, auf dem die Turtle zeichnet. "
"Für dieses Objekt können dann TurtleScreen-Methoden aufgerufen werden."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1564
msgid ""
">>> ts = turtle.getscreen()\n"
">>> ts\n"
"<turtle._Screen object at 0x...>\n"
">>> ts.bgcolor(\"pink\")"
msgstr ""
">>> ts = turtle.getscreen()\n"
">>> ts\n"
"<turtle._Screen object at 0x...>\n"
">>> ts.bgcolor(\"pink\")"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1577
msgid ""
"Set or disable the undo buffer. If *size* is an integer, an empty undo "
"buffer of the given size is installed. *size* is the maximum number of "
"turtle actions that can be undone by :func:`undo`. If *size* is ``None``, "
"the undo buffer is disabled."
msgstr ""
"Setze den Undo-Puffer oder deaktiviere ihn. Ist *size* eine Ganzzahl, wird "
"ein leerer Undo-Puffer der angegebenen Größe installiert. *size* gibt die "
"maximale Anzahl der Turtle-Aktionen an, die durch die Methode/"
"Funktion :func:`undo` rückgängig gemacht werden können. Ist *size* ``None``, "
"wird der Undo-Puffer deaktiviert."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1582
msgid ">>> turtle.setundobuffer(42)"
msgstr ">>> turtle.setundobuffer(42)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1590
msgid "Return the number of entries in the undo buffer."
msgstr "Gib die Anzahl der Einträge im Undo-Puffer zurück."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1592
msgid ""
">>> while undobufferentries():\n"
"...     undo()"
msgstr ""
">>> while undobufferentries():\n"
"...     undo()"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1603
msgid "Screen methods and functions"
msgstr "Screen-Methoden und -Funktionen"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1605
msgid ""
"Most of the examples in this section refer to a TurtleScreen instance called "
"``screen``."
msgstr ""
"Die meisten Beispiele in diesem Abschnitt beziehen sich auf eine "
"TurtleScreen-Instanz namens ``screen``."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1616
msgid "Window control"
msgstr "Fenstersteuerung"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1622
msgid "Return or set the background color of the TurtleScreen."
msgstr "Gib die Hintergrundfarbe des TurtleScreen zurück oder setze sie."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1626
msgid "``bgcolor()``"
msgstr "``bgcolor()``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1627
msgid ""
"Return the current background color as a color specification string or as a "
"tuple (see example).  May be used as input to "
"another :func:`color`, :func:`pencolor`, :func:`fillcolor` "
"or :func:`bgcolor` call."
msgstr ""
"Gib die aktuelle Hintergrundfarbe als Farbangabe-Zeichenkette oder als Tupel "
"zurück (siehe Beispiel). Kann als Eingabe für einen weiteren Aufruf "
"von :func:`color`, :func:`pencolor`, :func:`fillcolor` oder :func:`bgcolor` "
"verwendet werden."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1632
msgid "``bgcolor(colorstring)``"
msgstr "``bgcolor(colorstring)``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1633
msgid ""
"Set the background color to *colorstring*, which is a Tk color specification "
"string, such as ``\"red\"``, ``\"yellow\"``, or ``\"#33cc8c\"``."
msgstr ""
"Setzt die Hintergrundfarbe auf *colorstring*, eine Tk-Farbangabe als "
"Zeichenkette, etwa ``\"red\"``, ``\"yellow\"`` oder ``\"#33cc8c\"``."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1636
msgid "``bgcolor((r, g, b))``"
msgstr "``bgcolor((r, g, b))``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1637
msgid ""
"Set the background color to the RGB color represented by the tuple of *r*, "
"*g*, and *b*. Each of *r*, *g*, and *b* must be between 0 and colormode, "
"where colormode is either 1.0 or 255 (see :func:`colormode`)."
msgstr ""
"Setze die Hintergrundfarbe auf die durch das Tupel aus *r*, *g* und *b* "
"dargestellte RGB-Farbe. Jeder der Werte *r*, *g* und *b* muss im Bereich "
"0..colormode liegen, wobei colormode entweder 1.0 oder 255 ist "
"(siehe :func:`colormode`)."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1642
msgid "``bgcolor(r, g, b)``"
msgstr "``bgcolor(r, g, b)``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1643
msgid ""
"Set the background color to the RGB color represented by *r*, *g*, and *b*. "
"Each of *r*, *g*, and *b* must be between 0 and colormode."
msgstr ""
"Setze die Hintergrundfarbe auf die durch *r*, *g* und *b* dargestellte RGB-"
"Farbe. Jeder der Werte *r*, *g* und *b* muss im Bereich 0..colormode liegen."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1646
msgid ""
">>> screen.bgcolor(\"orange\")\n"
">>> screen.bgcolor()\n"
"'orange'\n"
">>> screen.bgcolor(\"#800080\")\n"
">>> screen.bgcolor()\n"
"(128.0, 0.0, 128.0)"
msgstr ""
">>> screen.bgcolor(\"orange\")\n"
">>> screen.bgcolor()\n"
"'orange'\n"
">>> screen.bgcolor(\"#800080\")\n"
">>> screen.bgcolor()\n"
"(128.0, 0.0, 128.0)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1661
msgid ""
"Set the background image or return the name of the current one. If *picname* "
"is the name of an image file (PNG, GIF, PGM, and PPM), set that image as the "
"background. If *picname* is ``\"nopic\"``, delete the background image, if "
"present. If *picname* is ``None``, return the filename of the current "
"background image. ::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1667
msgid ""
">>> screen.bgpic()\n"
"'nopic'\n"
">>> screen.bgpic(\"landscape.gif\")\n"
">>> screen.bgpic()\n"
"'landscape.gif'"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1678
msgid ""
"This TurtleScreen method is available as a global function only under the "
"name ``clearscreen``.  The global function ``clear`` is a different one "
"derived from the Turtle method ``clear``."
msgstr ""
"Diese TurtleScreen-Methode ist als globale Funktion nur unter dem Namen "
"``clearscreen`` verfügbar. Die globale Funktion ``clear`` ist eine andere, "
"die von der Turtle-Methode ``clear`` abgeleitet ist."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1685
msgid ""
"Delete all drawings and all turtles from the TurtleScreen.  Reset the now "
"empty TurtleScreen to its initial state: white background, no background "
"image, no event bindings and tracing on."
msgstr ""
"Lösche alle Zeichnungen und alle Turtles vom TurtleScreen. Setze den nun "
"leeren TurtleScreen auf seinen Ausgangszustand zurück: weißer Hintergrund, "
"kein Hintergrundbild, keine Ereignisbindungen und Tracing aktiviert."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1694
msgid ""
"This TurtleScreen method is available as a global function only under the "
"name ``resetscreen``.  The global function ``reset`` is another one derived "
"from the Turtle method ``reset``."
msgstr ""
"Diese TurtleScreen-Methode ist als globale Funktion nur unter dem Namen "
"``resetscreen`` verfügbar. Die globale Funktion ``reset`` ist eine andere, "
"die von der Turtle-Methode ``reset`` abgeleitet ist."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1701
msgid "Reset all turtles on the screen to their initial state."
msgstr "Setze alle Turtles auf dem Screen auf ihren Ausgangszustand zurück."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1708
msgid "a colorstring or a color tuple or ``None``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1710
msgid ""
"Resize the canvas the turtles are drawing on. *canvwidth* and *canvheight* "
"are the new width and height of the canvas in pixels, and *bg* is the new "
"background color. If no arguments are given, return the current canvas width "
"and height."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1715
msgid ""
"The drawing window is not altered. To see hidden parts of the canvas, use "
"the scrollbars. This can make visible those parts of a drawing which were "
"outside the canvas before, for example to find a turtle that has wandered "
"off the canvas."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1720
msgid ""
">>> screen.screensize()\n"
"(400, 300)\n"
">>> screen.screensize(2000,1500)\n"
">>> screen.screensize()\n"
"(2000, 1500)"
msgstr ""
">>> screen.screensize()\n"
"(400, 300)\n"
">>> screen.screensize(2000,1500)\n"
">>> screen.screensize()\n"
"(2000, 1500)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1737
msgid ""
"Set up a user-defined coordinate system. *llx* and *lly* are the x and y "
"coordinates of the lower left corner of the canvas. *urx* and *ury* are the "
"x and y coordinates of the upper right corner. Switch to mode \"world\" if "
"necessary, which performs a reset. If mode \"world\" is already active, all "
"drawings are redrawn according to the new coordinates. In user-defined "
"coordinate systems, angles may appear distorted, see :func:`mode`."
msgstr ""
"Richte ein benutzerdefiniertes Koordinatensystem ein. *llx* und *lly* sind "
"die x- und die y-Koordinate der linken unteren Ecke der Leinwand. *urx* und "
"*ury* sind die x- und die y-Koordinate der rechten oberen Ecke. Wechselt "
"nötigenfalls in den Modus \"world\", was ein Zurücksetzen auslöst. Ist der "
"Modus \"world\" schon aktiv, werden alle Zeichnungen gemäß den neuen "
"Koordinaten neu gezeichnet. In benutzerdefinierten Koordinatensystemen "
"können Winkel verzerrt erscheinen, siehe :func:`mode`."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1744
msgid ""
">>> screen.reset()\n"
">>> screen.setworldcoordinates(-50,-7.5,50,7.5)\n"
">>> for _ in range(72):\n"
"...     left(10)\n"
"...\n"
">>> for _ in range(8):\n"
"...     left(45); fd(2)   # a regular octagon"
msgstr ""
">>> screen.reset()\n"
">>> screen.setworldcoordinates(-50,-7.5,50,7.5)\n"
">>> for _ in range(72):\n"
"...     left(10)\n"
"...\n"
">>> for _ in range(8):\n"
"...     left(45); fd(2)   # a regular octagon"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1765
msgid "Animation control"
msgstr "Animationskontrolle"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1769
msgid ""
"Temporarily turn off turtle animation. The code inside the :keyword:`with` "
"block is not animated. Once the block is exited, the drawing appears. This "
"is useful for drawing complex shapes where even the fastest speed setting is "
"too slow."
msgstr ""
"Schalte die Turtle-Animation vorübergehend ab. Der Code innerhalb "
"des :keyword:`with`-Blocks wird nicht animiert. Sobald der Block verlassen "
"wird, erscheint die Zeichnung. Das ist nützlich, um aufwendige Formen zu "
"zeichnen, bei denen selbst die schnellste Geschwindigkeitseinstellung zu "
"langsam ist."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1774
msgid ""
">>> with screen.no_animation():\n"
"...     for dist in range(2, 400, 2):\n"
"...         fd(dist)\n"
"...         rt(90)"
msgstr ""
">>> with screen.no_animation():\n"
"...     for dist in range(2, 400, 2):\n"
"...         fd(dist)\n"
"...         rt(90)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1787 ../../library/turtle.rst:1805
#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1806
msgid "a nonnegative integer or ``None``"
msgstr "eine nichtnegative Ganzzahl oder ``None``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1789
msgid ""
"Return or set the drawing delay in milliseconds. This is approximately the "
"time interval between two consecutive canvas updates. The longer the drawing "
"delay, the slower the animation."
msgstr ""
"Gib die Zeichenverzögerung in Millisekunden zurück oder setze sie. Das ist "
"ungefähr das Zeitintervall zwischen zwei aufeinanderfolgenden "
"Aktualisierungen der Leinwand. Je länger die Zeichenverzögerung, desto "
"langsamer die Animation."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1793
msgid ""
">>> screen.delay()\n"
"10\n"
">>> screen.delay(5)\n"
">>> screen.delay()\n"
"5"
msgstr ""
">>> screen.delay()\n"
"10\n"
">>> screen.delay(5)\n"
">>> screen.delay()\n"
"5"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1808
msgid ""
"Turn turtle animation on or off and set the drawing delay. If *n* is given, "
"only every n-th regular screen update is performed, which can be used to "
"speed up the drawing of complex graphics. If *n* is 0, animation is turned "
"off and the screen is only updated by calling :func:`update`. If *delay* is "
"given, it sets the drawing delay, see :func:`delay`. When called without "
"arguments, return the current value of *n*."
msgstr ""
"Schalte die Turtle-Animation ein oder aus und setze die Zeichenverzögerung. "
"Wird *n* angegeben, wird nur jede n-te gewöhnliche Bildschirmaktualisierung "
"ausgeführt, womit sich das Zeichnen aufwendiger Grafiken beschleunigen "
"lässt. Ist *n* 0, wird die Animation abgeschaltet und der Bildschirm nur "
"noch durch einen Aufruf von :func:`update` aktualisiert. Wird *delay* "
"angegeben, setzt es die Zeichenverzögerung, siehe :func:`delay`. Beim Aufruf "
"ohne Argumente wird der aktuelle Wert von *n* zurückgegeben."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1815
msgid ""
">>> screen.tracer(8, 25)\n"
">>> dist = 2\n"
">>> for i in range(200):\n"
"...     fd(dist)\n"
"...     rt(90)\n"
"...     dist += 2"
msgstr ""
">>> screen.tracer(8, 25)\n"
">>> dist = 2\n"
">>> for i in range(200):\n"
"...     fd(dist)\n"
"...     rt(90)\n"
"...     dist += 2"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1828
msgid "Perform a TurtleScreen update. To be used when tracer is turned off."
msgstr ""
"Führe eine TurtleScreen-Aktualisierung durch. Zu verwenden, wenn tracer "
"ausgeschaltet ist."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1830
msgid "See also the RawTurtle/Turtle method :func:`speed`."
msgstr "Siehe auch die RawTurtle/Turtle-Methode :func:`speed`."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1834
msgid "Using screen events"
msgstr "Screen-Events verwenden"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1838 ../../library/turtle.rst:1839
msgid "ignored"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1841
msgid ""
"Set focus on the :class:`TurtleScreen` so that it receives key events. The "
"two dummy arguments are only there so that :func:`listen` can be passed "
"to :func:`onclick`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1849 ../../library/turtle.rst:1873
msgid "a function with no arguments or ``None``"
msgstr "eine Funktion ohne Argumente oder ``None``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1852
msgid ""
"Bind *fun* to the key-release event of *key*. *key* is a key, such as \"a\", "
"or a key symbol, such as \"space\". If *fun* is ``None``, the event binding "
"is removed. To be able to receive key events, the :class:`TurtleScreen` must "
"have focus, see :func:`listen`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1857
msgid ""
">>> def f():\n"
"...     fd(50)\n"
"...     lt(60)\n"
"...\n"
">>> screen.onkey(f, \"Up\")\n"
">>> screen.listen()"
msgstr ""
">>> def f():\n"
"...     fd(50)\n"
"...     lt(60)\n"
"...\n"
">>> screen.onkey(f, \"Up\")\n"
">>> screen.listen()"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1867
msgid ""
"The turtle can then be moved by repeatedly pressing the up-arrow key, "
"drawing a hexagon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1876
msgid ""
"Bind *fun* to the key-press event of *key*. *key* is a key, such as \"a\", "
"or a key symbol, such as \"space\". If *key* is not given, *fun* is bound to "
"the key-press event of any key. If *fun* is ``None``, the event binding is "
"removed. To be able to receive key events, the :class:`TurtleScreen` must "
"have focus, see :func:`listen`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1882
msgid ""
">>> def f():\n"
"...     fd(50)\n"
"...     lt(60)\n"
"...\n"
">>> screen.onkeypress(f, \"Up\")\n"
">>> screen.listen()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1892
msgid ""
"The turtle can then be moved by pressing or holding down the up-arrow key, "
"drawing a hexagon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1903
msgid ""
"Bind *fun* to mouse-click events on this screen. *fun* is called with the "
"coordinates of the clicked point on the canvas. If *fun* is ``None``, "
"existing bindings are removed. *btn* is the number of the mouse button and "
"defaults to 1, the left mouse button. If *add* is ``True``, a new binding is "
"added, otherwise it replaces a former binding."
msgstr ""
"Binde *fun* an Mausklick-Ereignisse auf diesem Screen. *fun* wird mit den "
"Koordinaten des angeklickten Punktes auf der Leinwand aufgerufen. Ist *fun* "
"``None``, werden bestehende Bindungen entfernt. *btn* ist die Nummer der "
"Maustaste und ist standardmäßig 1, die linke Maustaste. Ist *add* ``True``, "
"wird eine neue Bindung hinzugefügt, andernfalls ersetzt sie eine frühere "
"Bindung."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1909
msgid ""
"Example for a TurtleScreen instance named ``screen`` and a Turtle instance "
"named ``turtle``:"
msgstr ""
"Beispiel für eine TurtleScreen-Instanz namens ``screen`` und eine Turtle-"
"Instanz namens ``turtle``:"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1912
msgid ""
">>> screen.onclick(turtle.goto) # Subsequently clicking into the "
"TurtleScreen will\n"
">>>                             # make the turtle move to the clicked "
"point.\n"
">>> screen.onclick(None)        # remove event binding again"
msgstr ""
">>> screen.onclick(turtle.goto) # Subsequently clicking into the "
"TurtleScreen will\n"
">>>                             # make the turtle move to the clicked "
"point.\n"
">>> screen.onclick(None)        # remove event binding again"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1920
msgid ""
"This TurtleScreen method is available as a global function only under the "
"name ``onscreenclick``.  The global function ``onclick`` is another one "
"derived from the Turtle method ``onclick``."
msgstr ""
"Diese TurtleScreen-Methode ist als globale Funktion nur unter dem Namen "
"``onscreenclick`` verfügbar. Die globale Funktion ``onclick`` ist eine "
"andere, die von der Turtle-Methode ``onclick`` abgeleitet ist."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1927
msgid "a function with no arguments"
msgstr "eine Funktion ohne Argumente"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1928
msgid "a nonnegative number"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1930
msgid "Install a timer that calls *fun* after *t* milliseconds."
msgstr "Installiere einen Timer, der *fun* nach *t* Millisekunden aufruft."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1932
msgid ""
">>> running = True\n"
">>> def f():\n"
"...     if running:\n"
"...         fd(50)\n"
"...         lt(60)\n"
"...         screen.ontimer(f, 250)\n"
">>> f()  # makes the turtle march around\n"
">>> running = False"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1948
msgid ""
"Start the event loop by calling Tkinter's :meth:`~tkinter.Misc.mainloop` "
"method. Must be the last statement in a turtle graphics program. Must *not* "
"be used if a script is run from within IDLE in -n mode (see :ref:`idle-no-"
"subprocess`)."
msgstr ""
"Starte die Ereignisschleife, indem die "
"Methode :meth:`~tkinter.Misc.mainloop` von Tkinter aufgerufen wird. Muss die "
"letzte Anweisung in einem Turtle-Grafikprogramm sein. Darf *nicht* verwendet "
"werden, wenn ein Skript innerhalb von IDLE im Modus -n ausgeführt wird "
"(siehe :ref:`idle-no-subprocess`)."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1955
msgid "Input methods"
msgstr "Eingabemethoden"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1962
msgid ""
"Pop up a dialog window for input of a string. *title* is the title of the "
"dialog window and *prompt* is a text describing what information to input. "
"Return the string entered. If the dialog is canceled, return ``None``. ::"
msgstr ""
"Öffne ein Dialogfenster zur Eingabe einer Zeichenkette. *title* ist der "
"Titel des Dialogfensters, *prompt* ist ein Text, der beschreibt, welche "
"Information einzugeben ist. Gib die eingegebene Zeichenkette zurück. Wird "
"der Dialog abgebrochen, wird ``None`` zurückgegeben. ::"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1966
msgid ">>> screen.textinput(\"NIM\", \"Name of first player:\")"
msgstr ">>> screen.textinput(\"NIM\", \"Name of first player:\")"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1977
msgid ""
"Pop up a dialog window for input of a number. *title* is the title of the "
"dialog window and *prompt* is a text describing what numerical information "
"to input. *default* is the default value, *minval* and *maxval* are the "
"minimum and maximum values for input. If these are given, the number entered "
"must be between *minval* and *maxval*. If not, a hint is issued and the "
"dialog remains open for correction. Return the number entered. If the dialog "
"is canceled, return ``None``. ::"
msgstr ""
"Öffne ein Dialogfenster zur Eingabe einer Zahl. *title* ist der Titel des "
"Dialogfensters, *prompt* ist ein Text, der beschreibt, welche Zahlenangabe "
"einzugeben ist. *default* ist der Standardwert, *minval* und *maxval* sind "
"der Mindest- und der Höchstwert für die Eingabe. Sind diese angegeben, muss "
"die eingegebene Zahl zwischen *minval* und *maxval* liegen. Ist das nicht "
"der Fall, wird ein Hinweis ausgegeben und der Dialog bleibt zur Korrektur "
"geöffnet. Gib die eingegebene Zahl zurück. Wird der Dialog abgebrochen, wird "
"``None`` zurückgegeben. ::"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1985
msgid ""
">>> screen.numinput(\"Poker\", \"Your stakes:\", 1000, minval=10, "
"maxval=10000)"
msgstr ""
">>> screen.numinput(\"Poker\", \"Your stakes:\", 1000, minval=10, "
"maxval=10000)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1989
msgid "Settings and special methods"
msgstr "Einstellungen und spezielle Methoden"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1995
msgid ""
"Set the turtle mode and perform a reset. *mode* is one of the strings "
"\"standard\", \"logo\" or \"world\". If *mode* is not given, return the "
"current mode."
msgstr ""
"Setze den Turtle-Modus und führe ein Zurücksetzen durch. *mode* ist eine der "
"Zeichenketten \"standard\", \"logo\" oder \"world\". Wird *mode* nicht "
"angegeben, wird der aktuelle Modus zurückgegeben."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1999
msgid ""
"Mode \"standard\" is compatible with the old :mod:`!turtle` module. Mode "
"\"logo\" is compatible with most Logo turtle graphics. Mode \"world\" uses "
"user-defined world coordinates, see :func:`setworldcoordinates`. In this "
"mode, angles appear distorted if the x and y units are not of equal length."
msgstr ""
"Der Modus \"standard\" ist mit dem alten Modul :mod:`!turtle` verträglich. "
"Der Modus \"logo\" ist mit den meisten Logo-Turtle-Grafiken verträglich. Der "
"Modus \"world\" verwendet benutzerdefinierte Weltkoordinaten, "
"siehe :func:`setworldcoordinates`. In diesem Modus erscheinen Winkel "
"verzerrt, wenn die x- und die y-Einheit nicht gleich lang sind."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2005
msgid "Mode"
msgstr "Modus"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2005
msgid "Initial turtle heading"
msgstr "Anfängliche Ausrichtung der Turtle"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2005
msgid "positive angles"
msgstr "positive Winkel"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2007
msgid "\"standard\""
msgstr "\"standard\""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2007
msgid "to the right (east)"
msgstr "nach rechts (Osten)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2007
msgid "counterclockwise"
msgstr "gegen den Uhrzeigersinn"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2008
msgid "\"logo\""
msgstr "\"logo\""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2008
msgid "upward    (north)"
msgstr "nach oben    (Norden)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2008
msgid "clockwise"
msgstr "im Uhrzeigersinn"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2011
msgid ""
">>> mode(\"logo\")  # resets turtle heading to north\n"
">>> mode()\n"
"'logo'"
msgstr ""
">>> mode(\"logo\")  # resets turtle heading to north\n"
">>> mode()\n"
"'logo'"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2023
msgid ""
"Return the colormode or set it to 1.0 or 255. After setting it, the *r*, *g* "
"and *b* values of color triples have to be between 0 and *cmode*."
msgstr ""
"Gib den colormode zurück oder setze ihn auf 1.0 oder 255. Nach dem Setzen "
"müssen die Werte *r*, *g* und *b* von Farbtripeln zwischen 0 und *cmode* "
"liegen."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2026
msgid ""
">>> screen.colormode(1)\n"
">>> turtle.pencolor(240, 160, 80)\n"
"Traceback (most recent call last):\n"
"     ...\n"
"TurtleGraphicsError: bad color sequence: (240, 160, 80)\n"
">>> screen.colormode()\n"
"1.0\n"
">>> screen.colormode(255)\n"
">>> screen.colormode()\n"
"255\n"
">>> turtle.pencolor(240,160,80)"
msgstr ""
">>> screen.colormode(1)\n"
">>> turtle.pencolor(240, 160, 80)\n"
"Traceback (most recent call last):\n"
"     ...\n"
"TurtleGraphicsError: bad color sequence: (240, 160, 80)\n"
">>> screen.colormode()\n"
"1.0\n"
">>> screen.colormode(255)\n"
">>> screen.colormode()\n"
"255\n"
">>> turtle.pencolor(240,160,80)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2044
msgid ""
"Return the Canvas of this TurtleScreen.  Useful for insiders who know what "
"to do with a Tkinter Canvas."
msgstr ""
"Gib die Canvas dieses TurtleScreen zurück. Nützlich für Insider, die wissen, "
"was mit einer Tkinter-Canvas anzufangen ist."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2047
msgid ""
">>> cv = screen.getcanvas()\n"
">>> cv\n"
"<turtle.ScrolledCanvas object ...>"
msgstr ""
">>> cv = screen.getcanvas()\n"
">>> cv\n"
"<turtle.ScrolledCanvas object ...>"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2057
msgid "Return a list of names of all currently available turtle shapes."
msgstr ""
"Gib eine Liste der Namen aller aktuell verfügbaren Turtle-Formen zurück."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2059
msgid ""
">>> screen.getshapes()\n"
"['arrow', 'blank', 'circle', ..., 'turtle']"
msgstr ""
">>> screen.getshapes()\n"
"['arrow', 'blank', 'circle', ..., 'turtle']"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2070
msgid ""
"a string, a tuple of pairs of numbers, a :class:`Shape` object or ``None``"
msgstr ""
"eine Zeichenkette, ein Tupel aus Zahlenpaaren, ein :class:`Shape`-Objekt "
"oder ``None``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2073
msgid ""
"Add a turtle shape to the TurtleScreen's shape list. It can be called in "
"four different ways:"
msgstr ""
"Füge der Formenliste des TurtleScreen eine Turtle-Form hinzu. Das lässt sich "
"auf vier verschiedene Weisen aufrufen:"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2076
msgid ""
"*name* is the name of an image file (PNG, GIF, PGM, and PPM) and *shape* is "
"``None``: Install the corresponding image shape. ::"
msgstr ""
"*name* ist der Name einer Bilddatei (PNG, GIF, PGM und PPM) und *shape* ist "
"``None``: Installiere die entsprechende Bildform. ::"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2079
msgid ">>> screen.register_shape(\"turtle.gif\")"
msgstr ">>> screen.register_shape(\"turtle.gif\")"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2081
msgid ""
"*name* is an arbitrary string and *shape* is the name of an image file (PNG, "
"GIF, PGM, and PPM): Install the corresponding image shape. ::"
msgstr ""
"*name* ist eine beliebige Zeichenkette und *shape* ist der Name einer "
"Bilddatei (PNG, GIF, PGM und PPM): Installiere die entsprechende Bildform. ::"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2084
msgid ">>> screen.register_shape(\"turtle\", \"turtle.gif\")"
msgstr ">>> screen.register_shape(\"turtle\", \"turtle.gif\")"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2086
msgid ""
"*name* is an arbitrary string and *shape* is a tuple of pairs of "
"coordinates: Install the corresponding polygon shape."
msgstr ""
"*name* ist eine beliebige Zeichenkette und *shape* ist ein Tupel aus "
"Koordinatenpaaren: Installiere die entsprechende Polygonform."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2089
msgid ">>> screen.register_shape(\"triangle\", ((5,-3), (0,5), (-5,-3)))"
msgstr ">>> screen.register_shape(\"triangle\", ((5,-3), (0,5), (-5,-3)))"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2094
msgid ""
"*name* is an arbitrary string and *shape* is a (compound) :class:`Shape` "
"object: Install the corresponding compound shape."
msgstr ""
"*name* ist eine beliebige Zeichenkette und *shape* ist ein "
"(zusammengesetztes) :class:`Shape`-Objekt: Installiere die entsprechende "
"zusammengesetzte Form."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2097
msgid ""
"Image shapes do not rotate when turning the turtle, so they do not display "
"the heading of the turtle. To use a registered shape, call :func:`shape` "
"with its name."
msgstr ""
"Bildformen drehen sich nicht mit, wenn die Turtle gedreht wird, sie zeigen "
"also nicht die Ausrichtung der Turtle an. Um eine registrierte Form zu "
"verwenden, rufe :func:`shape` mit ihrem Namen auf."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2101
msgid ""
"Added support for PNG, PGM, and PPM image formats. Both a shape name and an "
"image file name can be specified."
msgstr ""
"Unterstützung für die Bildformate PNG, PGM und PPM hinzugefügt. Es kann "
"sowohl ein Formname als auch ein Bilddateiname angegeben werden."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2108
msgid "Return the list of turtles on the screen."
msgstr "Gib die Liste der Turtles auf dem Screen zurück."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2110
msgid ""
">>> for turtle in screen.turtles():\n"
"...     turtle.color(\"red\")"
msgstr ""
">>> for turtle in screen.turtles():\n"
"...     turtle.color(\"red\")"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2119
msgid "Return the height of the turtle window. ::"
msgstr "Gib die Höhe des Turtle-Fensters zurück. ::"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2121
msgid ""
">>> screen.window_height()\n"
"480"
msgstr ""
">>> screen.window_height()\n"
"480"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2127
msgid "Return the width of the turtle window. ::"
msgstr "Gib die Weite des Turtle-Fensters zurück. ::"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2129
msgid ""
">>> screen.window_width()\n"
"640"
msgstr ""
">>> screen.window_width()\n"
"640"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2137
msgid "Screen-only methods"
msgstr "Methoden, die es nur beim Screen gibt"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2141
msgid "Close the turtle graphics window."
msgstr "Schließe das Turtle-Grafikfenster."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2146
msgid "Bind ``bye()`` method to mouse clicks on the Screen."
msgstr "Binde die Methode ``bye()`` an Mausklicks auf dem Screen."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2149
msgid ""
"If the value \"using_IDLE\" in the configuration dictionary is ``False`` "
"(default value), also enter mainloop.  Remark: If IDLE with the ``-n`` "
"switch (no subprocess) is used, this value should be set to ``True`` "
"in :file:`turtle.cfg`.  In this case IDLE's own mainloop is active also for "
"the client script."
msgstr ""
"Ist der Wert \"using_IDLE\" im Konfigurations-Dictionary ``False`` "
"(Standardwert), wird auch mainloop aufgerufen. Anmerkung: Wird IDLE mit dem "
"Schalter ``-n`` (kein Subprozess) verwendet, sollte dieser Wert "
"in :file:`turtle.cfg` auf ``True`` gesetzt werden. In diesem Fall ist IDLEs "
"eigene mainloop auch für das Client-Skript aktiv."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2161
msgid ""
"Save the current drawing and the turtles as a PostScript file. *filename* is "
"the path of the file to create. It must end with ``\".ps\"`` or "
"``\".eps\"``. If a file with that name already exists, "
"a :exc:`FileExistsError` is raised, unless *overwrite* is ``True``. "
"*overwrite* must be given by name, as in ``overwrite=True``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2167
msgid ""
">>> screen.save(\"my_drawing.ps\")\n"
">>> screen.save(\"my_drawing.ps\", overwrite=True)"
msgstr ""
">>> screen.save(\"my_drawing.ps\")\n"
">>> screen.save(\"my_drawing.ps\", overwrite=True)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2178
msgid ""
"Set the size and position of the main window.  Default values of arguments "
"are stored in the configuration dictionary and can be changed via "
"a :file:`turtle.cfg` file."
msgstr ""
"Setze die Größe und Position des Hauptfensters. Standardwerte der Argumente "
"sind im Konfigurations-Dictionary gespeichert und können über "
"eine :file:`turtle.cfg`-Datei geändert werden."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2182
msgid ""
"if an integer, a size in pixels, if a float, a fraction of the screen; "
"default is 50% of screen"
msgstr ""
"bei einer Ganzzahl eine Größe in Pixeln, bei einer Gleitkommazahl ein Anteil "
"des Bildschirms; Standard ist 50 % des Bildschirms"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2184
msgid ""
"if an integer, the height in pixels, if a float, a fraction of the screen; "
"default is 75% of screen"
msgstr ""
"bei einer Ganzzahl die Höhe in Pixeln, bei einer Gleitkommazahl ein Anteil "
"des Bildschirms; Standard ist 75 % des Bildschirms"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2186
msgid ""
"if positive, starting position in pixels from the left edge of the screen, "
"if negative from the right edge, if ``None``, center window horizontally"
msgstr ""
"bei einem positiven Wert die Startposition in Pixeln vom linken "
"Bildschirmrand aus, bei einem negativen Wert vom rechten Rand aus, bei "
"``None`` wird das Fenster horizontal zentriert"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2189
msgid ""
"if positive, starting position in pixels from the top edge of the screen, if "
"negative from the bottom edge, if ``None``, center window vertically"
msgstr ""
"bei einem positiven Wert die Startposition in Pixeln vom oberen "
"Bildschirmrand aus, bei einem negativen Wert vom unteren Rand aus, bei "
"``None`` wird das Fenster vertikal zentriert"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2193
msgid ""
">>> screen.setup (width=200, height=200, startx=0, starty=0)\n"
">>>              # sets window to 200x200 pixels, in upper left of screen\n"
">>> screen.setup(width=.75, height=0.5, startx=None, starty=None)\n"
">>>              # sets window to 75% of screen by 50% of screen and centers"
msgstr ""
">>> screen.setup (width=200, height=200, startx=0, starty=0)\n"
">>>              # sets window to 200x200 pixels, in upper left of screen\n"
">>> screen.setup(width=.75, height=0.5, startx=None, starty=None)\n"
">>>              # sets window to 75% of screen by 50% of screen and centers"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2206
msgid ""
"Set the title of the turtle window to *titlestring*. The title is shown in "
"the title bar of the turtle graphics window."
msgstr ""
"Setze den Titel des Turtle-Fensters auf *titlestring*. Der Titel wird in der "
"Titelleiste des Turtle-Grafikfensters angezeigt."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2209
msgid ">>> screen.title(\"Welcome to the turtle zoo!\")"
msgstr ">>> screen.title(\"Welcome to the turtle zoo!\")"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2216
msgid "Public classes"
msgstr "Öffentliche Klassen"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2221
msgid ""
"a :class:`!tkinter.Canvas`, a :class:`ScrolledCanvas` or "
"a :class:`TurtleScreen`"
msgstr ""
"ein :class:`!tkinter.Canvas`, ein :class:`ScrolledCanvas` oder "
"ein :class:`TurtleScreen`"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2224
msgid ""
"Create a turtle.  The turtle has all methods described above as \"methods of "
"Turtle/RawTurtle\"."
msgstr ""
"Erstelle eine Turtle. Die Turtle hat alle oben als \"Methoden von Turtle/"
"RawTurtle\" beschriebenen Methoden."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2230
msgid ""
"Subclass of RawTurtle, has the same interface but draws on a "
"default :class:`Screen` object created automatically when needed for the "
"first time."
msgstr ""
"Unterklasse von RawTurtle, hat dieselbe Schnittstelle, zeichnet aber auf "
"einem Standard-:class:`Screen`-Objekt, das automatisch erstellt wird, wenn "
"es zum ersten Mal benötigt wird."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2236
msgid "a :class:`!tkinter.Canvas`"
msgstr "a :class:`!tkinter.Canvas`"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2238
msgid ""
"Provides screen oriented methods like :func:`bgcolor` etc. that are "
"described above."
msgstr ""
"Stellt bildschirmorientierte Methoden wie :func:`bgcolor` usw. bereit, die "
"oben beschrieben sind."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2244
msgid ""
"Subclass of :class:`TurtleScreen`, with :ref:`four methods added "
"<screenspecific>`. Calling ``Screen()`` returns the single screen object. If "
"it does not exist yet, it is created. Otherwise the existing one is returned."
msgstr ""
"Unterklasse von :class:`TurtleScreen`, mit :ref:`vier zusätzlichen Methoden "
"<screenspecific>`. Ein Aufruf von ``Screen()`` gibt das einzige Screen-"
"Objekt zurück. Existiert es noch nicht, wird es erzeugt. Andernfalls wird "
"das vorhandene zurückgegeben."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2252
msgid ""
"some Tkinter widget to contain the ScrolledCanvas, i.e. a Tkinter-canvas "
"with scrollbars added"
msgstr ""
"ein Tkinter-Widget, das den ScrolledCanvas enthält, d. h. ein Tkinter-Canvas "
"mit hinzugefügten Bildlaufleisten"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2255
msgid ""
"Used by class Screen, which thus automatically provides a ScrolledCanvas as "
"playground for the turtles."
msgstr ""
"Wird von der Klasse Screen verwendet, die dadurch automatisch einen "
"ScrolledCanvas als Spielfläche für die Turtles bereitstellt."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2261
msgid "depends on *type_*"
msgstr "hängt von *type_* ab"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2263
msgid ""
"Data structure modeling shapes. *type_* is one of the strings \"polygon\", "
"\"image\" or \"compound\". What *data* must be depends on *type_*: for "
"\"polygon\" a tuple of pairs of coordinates, for \"image\" an image (only "
"used internally), and for \"compound\" ``None``, as a compound shape is "
"built up using the :meth:`addcomponent` method."
msgstr ""
"Datenstruktur, die Formen nachbildet. *type_* ist eine der Zeichenketten "
"\"polygon\", \"image\" oder \"compound\". Was *data* sein muss, hängt von "
"*type_* ab: bei \"polygon\" ein Tupel aus Koordinatenpaaren, bei \"image\" "
"ein Bild (wird nur intern verwendet) und bei \"compound\" ``None``, weil "
"eine zusammengesetzte Form über die Methode :meth:`addcomponent` aufgebaut "
"wird."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2271
msgid "a tuple of pairs of numbers"
msgstr "ein Tupel aus Zahlenpaaren"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2272
msgid "a color"
msgstr "eine Farbe"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2273
msgid "a color or ``None``"
msgstr "eine Farbe oder ``None``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2275
msgid ""
"Add a component to a shape of type \"compound\". *poly* is a polygon, a "
"tuple of pairs of numbers. *fill* is the color the polygon is filled with "
"and *outline* is the color of its outline. If *outline* is not given, *fill* "
"is used for it as well."
msgstr ""
"Füge einer Form des Typs \"compound\" eine Komponente hinzu. *poly* ist ein "
"Polygon, ein Tupel aus Zahlenpaaren. *fill* ist die Farbe, mit der das "
"Polygon gefüllt wird, und *outline* ist die Farbe seines Umrisses. Wird "
"*outline* nicht angegeben, wird dafür ebenfalls *fill* verwendet."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2280
msgid "Example:"
msgstr "Beispiel:"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2282
msgid ""
">>> poly = ((0,0), (10,-5), (0,10), (-10,-5))\n"
">>> s = Shape(\"compound\")\n"
">>> s.addcomponent(poly, \"red\", \"blue\")\n"
">>> # ... add more components and then use register_shape()"
msgstr ""
">>> poly = ((0,0), (10,-5), (0,10), (-10,-5))\n"
">>> s = Shape(\"compound\")\n"
">>> s.addcomponent(poly, \"red\", \"blue\")\n"
">>> # ... add more components and then use register_shape()"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2290
msgid "See :ref:`compoundshapes`."
msgstr "Siehe :ref:`compoundshapes`."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2295
msgid ""
"A two-dimensional vector class, used as a helper class for implementing "
"turtle graphics.  May be useful for turtle graphics programs too.  Derived "
"from tuple, so a vector is a tuple!"
msgstr ""
"Eine zweidimensionale Vektorklasse, die als Hilfsklasse zur Implementierung "
"von Turtle-Grafik dient. Kann auch für Turtle-Grafik-Programme selbst "
"nützlich sein. Von tuple abgeleitet, ein Vektor ist also ein Tupel!"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2299
msgid "Provides (for *a*, *b* vectors, *k* number):"
msgstr "Bietet (für Vektoren *a*, *b*, Zahl *k*):"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2301
msgid "``a + b`` vector addition"
msgstr "``a + b`` Vectoraddition"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2302
msgid "``a - b`` vector subtraction"
msgstr "``a - b`` Vectorsubtraction"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2303
msgid "``a * b`` inner product"
msgstr "``a * b`` Skalarprodukt"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2304
msgid "``k * a`` and ``a * k`` multiplication with scalar"
msgstr "``k * a`` und ``a * k`` Multiplikation mit Skalar"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2305
msgid "``abs(a)`` absolute value of a"
msgstr "``abs(a)`` Absolutwert von a"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2306
msgid "``a.rotate(angle)`` rotation"
msgstr "``a.rotate(angle)`` Rotation"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2310
msgid "Exceptions"
msgstr "Erklärungen"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2312
msgid "The :mod:`!turtle` module defines the following exception:"
msgstr "Das Modul :mod:`!turtle` definiert die folgende Ausnahme:"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2316
msgid ""
"Raised for invalid arguments or operations. For example, a malformed color "
"string:"
msgstr ""
"Wird bei ungültigen Argumenten oder Operationen ausgelöst. Zum Beispiel bei "
"einer fehlerhaften Farbzeichenkette:"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2319
msgid ""
">>> turtle.color(\"blau\")\n"
"Traceback (most recent call last):\n"
"    ...\n"
"turtle.TurtleGraphicsError: bad color string: blau"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.color(\"blau\")\n"
"Traceback (most recent call last):\n"
"    ...\n"
"turtle.TurtleGraphicsError: bad color string: blau"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2333
msgid "How-to guides"
msgstr "How-to-Anleitungen"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2335
msgid "This section covers some typical turtle use-cases and approaches."
msgstr ""
"Dieser Abschnitt behandelt einige typische Anwendungsfälle und "
"Vorgehensweisen für Turtle."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2341
msgid "How to automatically begin and end filling"
msgstr "Füllen automatisch beginnen und beenden"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2343
msgid ""
"Starting with Python 3.14, you can use the :func:`fill` :term:`context "
"manager` instead of :func:`begin_fill` and :func:`end_fill` to automatically "
"begin and end fill. Here is an example::"
msgstr ""
"Ab Python 3.14 kannst du den :term:`Kontextmanager <context "
"manager>` :func:`fill` anstelle von :func:`begin_fill` und :func:`end_fill` "
"verwenden, um das Füllen automatisch zu beginnen und zu beenden. Hier ist "
"ein Beispiel::"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2347
msgid ""
"with fill():\n"
"    for i in range(4):\n"
"        forward(100)\n"
"        right(90)\n"
"\n"
"forward(200)"
msgstr ""
"with fill():\n"
"    for i in range(4):\n"
"        forward(100)\n"
"        right(90)\n"
"\n"
"forward(200)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2354
msgid "The code above is equivalent to::"
msgstr "Der obige Code ist äquivalent zu::"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2356
msgid ""
"begin_fill()\n"
"for i in range(4):\n"
"    forward(100)\n"
"    right(90)\n"
"end_fill()\n"
"\n"
"forward(200)"
msgstr ""
"begin_fill()\n"
"for i in range(4):\n"
"    forward(100)\n"
"    right(90)\n"
"end_fill()\n"
"\n"
"forward(200)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2369
msgid "How to use compound shapes"
msgstr "Zusammengesetzte Formen verwenden"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2371
msgid ""
"To use compound turtle shapes, which consist of several polygons of "
"different color, you must use the helper class :class:`Shape` explicitly as "
"described below:"
msgstr ""
"Um zusammengesetzte Turtle-Formen zu verwenden, die aus mehreren Polygonen "
"unterschiedlicher Farbe bestehen, musst du die Hilfsklasse :class:`Shape` "
"explizit verwenden, wie unten beschrieben:"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2375
msgid "Create an empty :class:`Shape` object of type \"compound\"."
msgstr "Erstelle ein leeres :class:`Shape`-Objekt vom Typ \"compound\"."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2376
msgid ""
"Add as many components to this object as desired, using "
"the :meth:`~Shape.addcomponent` method."
msgstr ""
"Füge diesem Objekt beliebig viele Komponenten hinzu, indem du die "
"Methode :meth:`~Shape.addcomponent` verwendest."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2379
msgid "For example:"
msgstr "Zum Beispiel:"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2381
msgid ""
">>> s = Shape(\"compound\")\n"
">>> poly1 = ((0,0), (10,-5), (0,10), (-10,-5))\n"
">>> s.addcomponent(poly1, \"red\", \"blue\")\n"
">>> poly2 = ((0,0), (10,-5), (-10,-5))\n"
">>> s.addcomponent(poly2, \"blue\", \"red\")"
msgstr ""
">>> s = Shape(\"compound\")\n"
">>> poly1 = ((0,0), (10,-5), (0,10), (-10,-5))\n"
">>> s.addcomponent(poly1, \"red\", \"blue\")\n"
">>> poly2 = ((0,0), (10,-5), (-10,-5))\n"
">>> s.addcomponent(poly2, \"blue\", \"red\")"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2390
msgid "Now add the Shape to the Screen's shapelist and use it:"
msgstr "Füge nun die Shape zur Formenliste des Screens hinzu und verwende sie:"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2392
msgid ""
">>> register_shape(\"myshape\", s)\n"
">>> shape(\"myshape\")"
msgstr ""
">>> register_shape(\"myshape\", s)\n"
">>> shape(\"myshape\")"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2402
msgid "How to use the ``turtle`` module namespace"
msgstr "Das ``turtle``-Modul im eigenen Namensraum verwenden"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2404
msgid ""
"Using ``from turtle import *`` is convenient - but be warned that it imports "
"a rather large collection of objects, and if you're doing anything but "
"turtle graphics you run the risk of a name conflict (this becomes even more "
"an issue if you're using turtle graphics in a script where other modules "
"might be imported)."
msgstr ""
"Es ist praktisch, ``from turtle import *`` zu verwenden – aber sei gewarnt, "
"dass dadurch eine recht große Sammlung von Objekten importiert wird, und "
"wenn du irgendetwas außer Turtle-Grafik machst, läufst du Gefahr eines "
"Namenskonflikts (dies wird noch problematischer, wenn du Turtle-Grafik in "
"einem Skript verwendest, in dem auch andere Module importiert werden "
"könnten)."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2410
msgid ""
"The solution is to use ``import turtle`` - ``fd()`` becomes ``turtle.fd()``, "
"``width()`` becomes ``turtle.width()`` and so on. (If typing \"turtle\" over "
"and over again becomes tedious, use for example ``import turtle as t`` "
"instead.)"
msgstr ""
"Die Lösung besteht darin, ``import turtle`` zu verwenden - ``fd()`` wird zu "
"``turtle.fd()``, ``width()`` wird zu ``turtle.width()`` und so weiter. "
"(Falls es lästig wird, immer wieder \"turtle\" zu tippen, verwende "
"stattdessen zum Beispiel ``import turtle as t``.)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2419
msgid "How to use turtle graphics in a script"
msgstr "Turtle-Grafik in einem Skript verwenden"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2421
msgid ""
"It's recommended to use the ``turtle`` module namespace as described "
"immediately above, for example::"
msgstr ""
"Es wird empfohlen, den Namensraum des Moduls ``turtle`` wie unmittelbar oben "
"beschrieben zu verwenden, zum Beispiel::"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2424
msgid ""
"import turtle as t\n"
"from random import random\n"
"\n"
"for i in range(100):\n"
"    steps = int(random() * 100)\n"
"    angle = int(random() * 360)\n"
"    t.right(angle)\n"
"    t.fd(steps)"
msgstr ""
"import turtle as t\n"
"from random import random\n"
"\n"
"for i in range(100):\n"
"    steps = int(random() * 100)\n"
"    angle = int(random() * 360)\n"
"    t.right(angle)\n"
"    t.fd(steps)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2433
msgid ""
"Another step is also required though - as soon as the script ends, Python "
"will also close the turtle's window. Add::"
msgstr ""
"Ein weiterer Schritt ist jedoch ebenfalls erforderlich - sobald das Skript "
"endet, wird Python auch das Fenster der Turtle schließen. Füge Folgendes "
"hinzu::"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2436
msgid "t.mainloop()"
msgstr "t.mainloop()"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2438
msgid ""
"to the end of the script. The script will now wait to be dismissed and will "
"not exit until it is terminated, for example by closing the turtle graphics "
"window."
msgstr ""
"am Ende des Skripts. Das Skript wartet nun darauf, geschlossen zu werden, "
"und beendet sich nicht, bis es beendet wird, zum Beispiel durch Schließen "
"des Turtle-Grafikfensters."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2446
msgid "How to use object-oriented turtle graphics"
msgstr "Objektorientierte Turtle-Grafik verwenden"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2448
msgid ""
":ref:`Explanation of the object-oriented interface <turtle-explanation>`"
msgstr ""
":ref:`Erklärung der objektorientierten Schnittstelle <turtle-explanation>`"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2450
msgid ""
"Other than for very basic introductory purposes, or for trying things out as "
"quickly as possible, it's more usual and much more powerful to use the "
"object-oriented approach to turtle graphics. For example, this allows "
"multiple turtles on screen at once."
msgstr ""
"Abgesehen von sehr grundlegenden Einführungszwecken oder um Dinge so schnell "
"wie möglich auszuprobieren, ist es üblicher und deutlich leistungsfähiger, "
"den objektorientierten Ansatz für Turtle-Grafik zu verwenden. Dies "
"ermöglicht zum Beispiel mehrere Turtles gleichzeitig auf dem Bildschirm."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2455
msgid ""
"In this approach, the various turtle commands are methods of objects (mostly "
"of ``Turtle`` objects). You *can* use the object-oriented approach in the "
"shell, but it would be more typical in a Python script."
msgstr ""
"Bei diesem Ansatz sind die verschiedenen Turtle-Befehle Methoden von "
"Objekten (meist von ``Turtle``-Objekten). Du *kannst* den objektorientierten "
"Ansatz auch in der Shell verwenden, typischer wäre es aber in einem Python-"
"Skript."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2459
msgid "The example above then becomes::"
msgstr "Das obige Beispiel wird dann zu::"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2461
msgid ""
"from turtle import Turtle\n"
"from random import random\n"
"\n"
"t = Turtle()\n"
"for i in range(100):\n"
"    steps = int(random() * 100)\n"
"    angle = int(random() * 360)\n"
"    t.right(angle)\n"
"    t.fd(steps)\n"
"\n"
"t.screen.mainloop()"
msgstr ""
"from turtle import Turtle\n"
"from random import random\n"
"\n"
"t = Turtle()\n"
"for i in range(100):\n"
"    steps = int(random() * 100)\n"
"    angle = int(random() * 360)\n"
"    t.right(angle)\n"
"    t.fd(steps)\n"
"\n"
"t.screen.mainloop()"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2473
msgid ""
"Note the last line. ``t.screen`` is an instance of the :class:`Screen` that "
"a Turtle instance exists on; it's created automatically along with the "
"turtle."
msgstr ""
"Beachte die letzte Zeile. ``t.screen`` ist eine Instanz der :class:`Screen`, "
"auf der eine Turtle-Instanz existiert; sie wird automatisch zusammen mit der "
"Turtle erstellt."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2477
msgid "The turtle's screen can be customised, for example::"
msgstr "Der Turtle-Scree kann angepasst werden, zum Beispiel::"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2479
msgid ""
"t.screen.title('Object-oriented turtle demo')\n"
"t.screen.bgcolor(\"orange\")"
msgstr ""
"t.screen.title('Object-oriented turtle demo')\n"
"t.screen.bgcolor(\"orange\")"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2486
msgid "How to use :func:`!help`"
msgstr "Wie man :func:`!help` verwendet"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2488
msgid ""
"The public methods of the Screen and Turtle classes are documented "
"extensively via docstrings.  So these can be used as online-help via the "
"Python help facilities:"
msgstr ""
"Die öffentlichen Methoden der Klassen Screen und Turtle sind ausführlich "
"über Docstrings dokumentiert. Diese können daher über die Python-"
"Hilfefunktionen als Online-Hilfe verwendet werden:"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2492
msgid ""
"When using IDLE, tooltips show the signatures and first lines of the "
"docstrings of typed in function-/method calls."
msgstr ""
"Bei Verwendung von IDLE zeigen Tooltips die Signaturen und die ersten Zeilen "
"der Docstrings eingetippter Funktions-/Methodenaufrufe."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2495
msgid "Calling :func:`help` on methods or functions displays the docstrings::"
msgstr ""
"Der Aufruf von :func:`help` für Methoden oder Funktionen zeigt die "
"Docstrings an::"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2497
msgid ""
">>> help(Screen.bgcolor)\n"
"Help on method bgcolor in module turtle:\n"
"\n"
"bgcolor(self, *args) unbound turtle.Screen method\n"
"    Set or return backgroundcolor of the TurtleScreen.\n"
"\n"
"    Arguments (if given): a color string or three numbers\n"
"    in the range 0..colormode or a 3-tuple of such numbers.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"    >>> screen.bgcolor(\"orange\")\n"
"    >>> screen.bgcolor()\n"
"    \"orange\"\n"
"    >>> screen.bgcolor(0.5,0,0.5)\n"
"    >>> screen.bgcolor()\n"
"    \"#800080\"\n"
"\n"
">>> help(Turtle.penup)\n"
"Help on method penup in module turtle:\n"
"\n"
"penup(self) unbound turtle.Turtle method\n"
"    Pull the pen up -- no drawing when moving.\n"
"\n"
"    Aliases: penup | pu | up\n"
"\n"
"    No argument\n"
"\n"
"    >>> turtle.penup()"
msgstr ""
">>> help(Screen.bgcolor)\n"
"Help on method bgcolor in module turtle:\n"
"\n"
"bgcolor(self, *args) unbound turtle.Screen method\n"
"    Set or return backgroundcolor of the TurtleScreen.\n"
"\n"
"    Arguments (if given): a color string or three numbers\n"
"    in the range 0..colormode or a 3-tuple of such numbers.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"    >>> screen.bgcolor(\"orange\")\n"
"    >>> screen.bgcolor()\n"
"    \"orange\"\n"
"    >>> screen.bgcolor(0.5,0,0.5)\n"
"    >>> screen.bgcolor()\n"
"    \"#800080\"\n"
"\n"
">>> help(Turtle.penup)\n"
"Help on method penup in module turtle:\n"
"\n"
"penup(self) unbound turtle.Turtle method\n"
"    Pull the pen up -- no drawing when moving.\n"
"\n"
"    Aliases: penup | pu | up\n"
"\n"
"    No argument\n"
"\n"
"    >>> turtle.penup()"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:2526
msgid ""
"The docstrings of the functions which are derived from methods have a "
"modified form::"
msgstr ""
"Die Docstrings der Funktionen, die von Methoden abgeleitet sind, haben eine "
